{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>How good are your tents, O Jacob.</b> Houses of study. As in יֹשֵׁב אֹהָלִים (Genesis 25:27), and as in וְיִשְׁכֹּן בְּאָהֳלֵי שֵׁם (Genesis 9:27), and likewise וְהָיָה כָּל מְבַקֵּשׁ ה׳ יֵצֵא אֶל אֹהֶל מוֹעֵד (Exodus 33:7)." "<b>Your dwellings.</b> Synagogues and sanctuaries of El, set apart to establish His name there and to receive the prayer of those who pray. And he said <b>how good</b> because they not only benefit those who engage in them, but benefit the entire nation, as the name Jacob indicates — that it will remain in the wake and at the end of all things and not cease — and as the name Israel indicates — to strive with Elohim and with men (Genesis 32:29)."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:41:00.796206317Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}